l visits. DW reports 14 US/UK houses and flats totaling over €91m/$106m, acquired 2003-2017 through 36 front companies registered in tax havens, with the monarch described as the 'final beneficiary'/'you know who.' DW says the palace confirmed overseas properties were held for diplomatic visits and security, and that current knowledge did not show development aid was funneled to the palace. Sources describe offshore ownership as potentially legal and do not establish wrongdoing."}
